senses.gloss:
(II)--a son of Jaimini and father of Sutvan or Sunvan; learnt a सम्हिता of the साम वेद from him, divid- ed the अथर्व वेद into two divisions;
1: भा. XII. 6. ७५; Br. II. 1. १३; ३४. १३; ३५. ३१, ५५; वा. ६१. २६; Vi. III. 6. 2.
a pupil of व्यास, helped him in arranging the अथर्व वेद; in charge of the अथर्वान्गिरस् (Atharva Veda); Kabandha, the pupil of, to whom was given by him the whole of the अथर्व वेद। ^2 भा. I. 4. २२; XII. 6. ५३; 7. 1; वा. ६०. १३, १५; ६१. ४९; Vi. III. 4. 9; 6. 8-9.

(V)--a follower of वृत्र in his battle with Indra. Slain by Hari;
1: भा. VI. १०. २१; VIII. १०. ५७.
a son of Praheti, the राक्षस;
2: Br. III. 7. ९०.
the राक्षस king in IV Talam; served as calf when they milked the earth.
3: Ib. II. २०. ३३; ३६. २१९.

(III)--a son of लङ्कु;
1: वा. ६९. १२८, १६५.
resident of the fourth talam or gabhastalam;
2: Ib. ५०. ३२.
milked both milk and blood in कपालपात्र by which the राक्षसस् prosper;
3: Ib. ६२. १८४.
acted as calf when the राक्षसस् milked the cow-earth.
4: M. १०. २३.
